Fri Sep 11 06:50:58 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.9.58:
  * Python nested-function calls resolve per lexical scope instead
    of leaking to a same-named function elsewhere
  * submodule imports in PEP 420 namespace packages and bare-name
    sibling imports in flat script dirs now resolve
  * PHP aliased use imports key the binding on the alias
  * a directory literally named out is skipped as build output only
    with build-output evidence, real source out/ is kept
  * variable-held constant script paths in exec position resolve
  * SQL CREATE INDEX emits index nodes; Rust module-level
    static/const declarations extracted as nodes
  * TS export star no longer resolves to a same-named interface
    method; incremental rebuild keeps rationale/summary on
    source-path collisions
  * install skips unwritable always-on registration with a warning;
    labelling falls back to a run-time claude CLI; all extra gains
    psycopg[binary]
- Keep deselecting timing-fragile
  test_same_size_rewrite_in_one_tick_is_requeued: test and
  detect.py logic identical to 0.9.57, still racy on slower hosts

